sub:quote a prov:Entity;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fractastical/delphisci/2404c437f822e1c98420130cd01e7972acf3ac57/books/levin-papers/inputs/2019-boundary.txt#line=95,96>;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "I have previously suggested that a better strategy than cellular re-wiring at the genetic level may be to edit the pattern-homeostatic set point and let wild-type cells build to the new spec. For example, the ability to re-write target morphology in planarian regeneration was recently shown, by altering the bioelectric state in flatworms, without genomic editing, giving rise to permanently double-headed worms (Durant et al., 2017; Levin et al., 2018).".
